From 8f3886c3071d51eddd4387380103b5a2bcdf6207 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lijunlong <lijunlong@openresty.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:50:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] bugfix: clean pending operations in ordinary coroutines.

Cancel pending timers and cosocket operations before freeing session-owned
coroutine contexts, including ordinary coroutines without Lua registry
references. Previously, aborting a session or exiting with a nested
ngx.sleep could leave its timer in the Nginx tree and cause a heap
use-after-free.

Cover client abort and ngx.exit in content and preread, including nested
coroutines spanning context list parts. All four scenarios reproduce the
use-after-free in a pre-fix ASan build.

Validation: the new regression and related sleep, coroutine, preread,
and client-abort suites pass 766 assertions with 78 skipped under ASan.

Centmin Mod: vendored with the src/ hunk only, the README and t/ hunks
listed below are not included.
---
 README.md                         |  15 +++
 src/ngx_stream_lua_util.c         |   7 +-
 t/197-coroutine-request-cleanup.t | 171 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 191 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 t/197-coroutine-request-cleanup.t

diff --git a/src/ngx_stream_lua_util.c b/src/ngx_stream_lua_util.c
index 8c996658..8984d288 100644
--- a/src/ngx_stream_lua_util.c
+++ b/src/ngx_stream_lua_util.c
@@ -2795,11 +2795,14 @@ ngx_stream_lua_finalize_threads(ngx_stream_lua_request_t *r,
 
             coctx = &cc[i];
 
+            /* Plain coroutines have no registry reference, but can still
+             * own a pending timer or cosocket operation. Cancel those before
+             * their request-pool coctx is freed as well. */
+            ngx_stream_lua_cleanup_pending_operation(coctx);
+
             ref = coctx->co_ref;
 
             if (ref != LUA_NOREF) {
-                ngx_stream_lua_cleanup_pending_operation(coctx);
-
                 ngx_stream_lua_probe_thread_delete(r, coctx->co, ctx);
 
                 if (!inited) {
